## Detail

Progressive authoring means a user can start with a plain markdown memo, add a default font later, then add a default font, header, footer, section, or table style only when the document needs it. The backend should preserve that path. A PDF output is visual and final, but it should still reflect the same neutral document model used by the editable Word backend.

The paragraph spacing should be comfortable but not airy. Headings should be visibly stronger than body text. A horizontal rule should span the available text area and separate sections without looking like a row of typed characters.

